Important design decision, arrived at after a real failed attempt: first tried matching hand-slot crops against Supercell's official card catalog icon art (downloaded via perception/download_card_icons.py from the iconUrls already present in config/cards.json). This performed badly — all matches under 0.17 confidence, 3 of 4 wrong. Root cause, confirmed visually via debug_card_match.py: the catalog icons use different framing/zoom than the live hand-slot render, and don't include the card border + elixir-cost badge the hand UI overlays. Fix: abandoned catalog icons as the matching source entirely; templates are now built from real hand-slot screenshots via label_hand.py instead, so comparisons are pixel-consistent (same framing on both sides). This worked immediately — 1.000 confidence on a self-match, and critically, 0.98–0.999 confidence when tested against a completely different screenshot (different match, same 3 cards) — that second result is the one that actually proves the approach generalizes, not the trivial self-match one.

