Red/blue channel-swap bug found and fixed (2026-08-15): perception/capture.py's screenshot() previously returned RGB from PIL directly, but every cv2-based script in the project (card_detector, etc.) assumed BGR — the root cause of early templates looking "blue and yellow" instead of true colors. Fixed by converting RGB→BGR in capture.py itself. One-time repair tools: perception/fix_color_channels.py (fixed the channel order of every pre-fix file in place — a reversible swap, no data lost) and perception/cleanup_pre_fix_files.py (deleted the small set of pre-fix files that weren't safely repairable this way: literal seed.png files from migrate_templates.py's very first run, plus everything that was sitting in the unlabeled queue at the time — see that script's docstring for why those specifically couldn't just be channel-swapped back). Both are one-time/historical now; nothing currently in the repo is still affected.

