**Debugger integration, same session, per Duncan's explicit request**: `perception/debug_live.py` now runs a live `TowerStateTracker`, feeds its state into `unit_tracker.update()` every frame, boxes all 6 towers on the gameplay window (green/orange/red by HP%, dark-red "DESTROYED" once confirmed, orange "?" for an inactive-but-not-destroyed king tower), added a new "TOWERS" section to the Debug panel, added a `"towers"` key to the JSONL log schema, and reset the tower tracker alongside cycle/opponent tracking on `'r'`. Also confirmed (already true, not a new fix) per Duncan's specific request: once `TowerStateTracker` confirms a tower destroyed, that region is genuinely never read again (not just displayed differently) — verified with a dedicated test that mocks `read_tower` and asserts it's never called for a confirmed-destroyed tower, protecting against exactly the failure mode Duncan flagged (a troop walking through the now-empty patch of ground producing a false reading).

**First live-match test of the tower reader + debugger integration (2026-08-20), two real bugs found in the same log and both fixed same day:**

1. **Both enemy princess towers falsely confirmed "destroyed" by frame 5 (0.72s into the session)** — traced directly in the log: `enemy_left`/`enemy_right` read `hp=None` for the first 4 frames, then flipped permanently to `destroyed=True` at frame 5. Far too early for real combat to have destroyed a tower — almost certainly a startup/loading transient (the game/UI not fully settled in the very first captured frames) satisfying the old `DESTROYED_CONFIRM_FRAMES=5` window, which is under a second at this project's realistic framerates. Because `destroyed` is permanent by design, this silently corrupted the rest of the match for anything consuming tower state (the new zone classifier included). Fixed by raising `DESTROYED_CONFIRM_FRAMES` 5 → 60 — the cost/benefit is deeply asymmetric (a false positive permanently corrupts everything downstream; a false negative just delays confirming a real destruction by a few extra seconds, costing nothing).
2. **`ally_left` intermittently read `hp=0.0` while NOT destroyed** — traced to a real, repeating pattern on `enemy_king` too (which was under sustained real attack in this match): a steady, correct HP reading would flash to exactly `0.0` for a single frame, then immediately revert — almost certainly a hit-flash VFX artifact briefly shifting the bar's color. There was no debounce on the continuous `hp_fraction` VALUE at all before this (only on the discrete `destroyed` signal), so a single noisy frame passed straight through to the panel/log. Fixed with the same debounce pattern already used elsewhere in this project (`HP_CONFIRM_FRAMES=2`, `HP_AGREEMENT_TOLERANCE=0.08`) — a new reading only updates the reported value once a second consecutive reading agrees with it.

Both fixed with 2 new dedicated tests reproducing the exact real patterns (a lone spurious reading not updating the value; a 5-frame miss streak — the old threshold — no longer falsely confirming destroyed) — `perception/test_tower_reader.py` is 8 tests now, all passing.

