`enemy_right` princess tower's `hp_fraction` read exactly `0.0` continuously for ~16 real seconds (frames 295–417 in `logs/debug_live_20260820_014617.jsonl`) before `destroyed` finally confirmed — Duncan's live impression matches this exactly: towers appear to read 0% "the instant they take damage" despite not being destroyed, while destruction itself (once it actually happens) gets confirmed correctly (~1s, consistent with today's `DESTROYED_CONFIRM_FRAMES=60` fix working as intended). **Root cause found and fixed** once Duncan supplied a real capture of `ally_left` at ~90%+ HP reading 0%: `_best_row` was picking a dark BORDER/bezel pixel row (present at every HP level, not a real fill state) instead of the true bar row, because the princess-ally `EMPTY_BGR` value was an unverified guess (borrowed from `side_reader.py`'s badge colors by analogy) that happened to closely match that border row's color — at 100% health the true fill row still won the "best row" competition, but the instant any real damage occurred, the always-present border row won instead, giving a false 0% regardless of true HP. Fixed with a REAL measurement from the capture: a clean, unambiguous fill→empty transition at ~91% width, confirmed consistent across two separate rows, matching Duncan's own "~90+%" estimate almost exactly. `perception/test_tower_reader.py` is 9 tests now (new: `test_real_damaged_princess_tower_reads_the_true_partial_fill`, locking in the real 0.91 value against regression), all passing — new fixture saved at `assets/tower_reader_calibration/ally_left_princess_damaged.png`. The princess-*enemy* `EMPTY_BGR` entry uses the same "borrowed/incidental" methodology and hasn't shown a similar bug yet, but deserves the same scrutiny if one ever does.

